# >>> repo-harness:gitignore-private-boundary >>>
# Maintainer notes — not part of the project; they live in the private notes repo,
# reachable through the `local` symlink. NO trailing slash on any path in this block:
# a worktree materializes these paths as SYMLINKS, and a `foo/` pattern matches a real
# directory only — the ignore then keeps working in the main tree and silently fails
# in every worktree.
/local

# Environment secrets and the per-machine agent sandbox config. `.env.*` covers the
# variants a real session produces — `.env.local`, and above all the `.env.bak.<epoch>`
# an editor or a script leaves behind. One of those sat untracked in a repo for weeks:
# the pre-commit secret scan only reads what is staged, so a secret nobody stages is a
# secret nobody scans, and `.env` alone does not match it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.ai-jail
# <<< repo-harness:gitignore-private-boundary <<<

# The built binary. `go build` with no -o drops it at the repo root under the module
# name, so a routine build leaves an 8 MB artifact one `git add -A` from being tracked.
/llmux

# The attempt log. LLMUX_LOG_PATH is an absolute path in a real deployment, but a
# development run points it inside the checkout, and SQLite's WAL and shared-memory
# sidecars appear next to the database rather than inside it.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Issue-tracker state. The backlog is maintainer material: it records what is being
# considered, abandoned and reordered, which is a different document from a statement
# of direction. ROADMAP.md is the part written for whoever arrives. No trailing slash,
# for the same reason the block above gives.
/.beads
/.bv

# The reservation-guard plugin, generated per machine. `.githooks/pre-commit` is a
# chain runner: it executes every plugin in `hooks.d/pre-commit/` and then the
# preserved original hook, so the secret scan still runs last and a checkout with no
# plugins behaves exactly as it did before. The plugin itself is not shareable, because
# the generator writes the absolute path of one machine's reservation store into it, and
# it is inert anywhere else regardless: it exits zero unless GIT_IDENTITY_ENABLED is set
# in the environment of whoever runs the commit. The Windows shims are install artifacts
# of the same generator.
/.githooks/hooks.d
/.githooks/pre-commit.cmd
/.githooks/pre-commit.ps1
/.githooks/pre-commit.orig
/.ntm/

# Per-repository agent harness configuration. Both directories are machine state rather
# than project state: the Claude side carries a permission allowlist naming absolute paths
# outside this checkout, and the Codex side wires a coordination server that only exists
# while a swarm is running on this host. Neither is required to build, test or run llmux,
# so a cloner loses nothing by not receiving them, and this repository is public.
#
# The Codex file reads its bearer token from MCP_AGENT_MAIL_TOKEN rather than carrying it
# inline. That remains the right shape now that the file is ignored: an ignored file is one
# `git add -f` away from being committed, and a credential that never enters the tree cannot
# be committed by accident at all.
/.claude/
/.codex/
